cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ice-cfd-validation-assistant in academic research, CFD verification reports, or engineering publications, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ice-cfd-validation-assistant: Open-Source 0D/1D ICE Thermodynamic Diagnostics, High-Altitude Aero-Diesel Spray Physics, Auto-Ignition Kinetics, Second-Law Exergy Budgets, and ASME V&V 20-2009 3D CFD Validation Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Strictly SI-normalized, vectorized Python 3.11+ engineering library for
  post-processing ANSYS Forte 3D internal combustion engine CFD simulations and
  Sandia Engine Combustion Network (ECN) spray datasets. Provides automated
  unit-safe ingestion, zero-phase pressure filtering, 4th-order non-uniform
  differentiation, 14-coefficient (2x7-term) NASA Glenn thermodynamic polynomials, Woschni
  and Hohenberg wall heat-transfer models, Heywood single-zone First-Law
  apparent and gross heat release rate (AHRR), sub-degree CA10/CA50/CA90 MFB
  extraction, MAPO and Eng (2002) acoustic Ringing Intensity, ISO 2533 Standard
  Atmosphere scaling, Hiroyasu-Arai (1990) and Naber-Siebers (1996) / Siebers
  (1999) high-altitude spray penetration and wall-impingement risk assessment,
  Wolfer (1938), Assanis (2003), and Hardenberg-Hase (1979) auto-ignition delay,
  dynamic Livengood-Wu (1955) auto-ignition integral with Hermite sub-grid root solving,
  two-stage LTHR/HTHR cool-flame detection, altitude-dependent dead state Second-Law
  thermomechanical exergy, Kotas (1995) chemical exergy, Gouy-Stodola irreversibility,
  closed-cycle exergy budgets, ASME V&V 20-2009 / Celik et al. (2008) three-grid Grid
  Convergence Index (GCI) with AMR oscillatory convergence protection, and 300-DPI SAE/IEEE
  publication plotting.
authors:
